%U A398475 1121207866121981309179,468743944343835142325837,277856681036927131921206050,233378319509658918694112520339,277614291786782460489563114534833
%N A398475 Number of right-Euclidean relations on an n-element labeled set having no isolated nonreflexive elements.
%C A398475 A relation R is right-Euclidean if xRy and xRz imply yRz for all x, y, z. An isolated nonreflexive element is an element x such that x is unrelated to every element, including itself.
%C A398475 For n >= 1, a(n) is also the number of serial right-Euclidean relations on an n-element labeled set. A relation R is serial if for every x there exists y such that xRy. For right-Euclidean relations, seriality is equivalent to having no isolated nonreflexive elements.
%F A398475 E.g.f.: exp(Sum_{k>=1} x^k*exp((2^k-1)*x)/k!).
%F A398475 Exponential transform of A001831.
%e A398475 For n = 2, the 4 relations are {(1,1),(2,1)}, {(1,1),(2,2)}, {(1,2),(2,2)}, and {(1,1),(1,2),(2,1),(2,2)}.
%e A398475 For n = 3, a(3) = A001831(3) + 3*A001831(2)*A001831(1) + A001831(1)^3 = 13 + 9 + 1 = 23.
%Y A398475 Cf. A001831.
%K A398475 nonn,new
%O A398475 0,3
